//      where the nucleoid is deepest behind it.
//      The DnaB helicase (PDB 6QEL), a ring round the lagging strand, unwinds the parent DNA. DNA polymerase III (5FKV), held on by its
//      β clamp, copies the leading strand without stopping. The lagging strand loops out, coated by SSB (1EYG), and is copied the other
//      way in Okazaki fragments of 1,000–2,000 bases, each begun from a short RNA primer laid by primase (DnaG, 1DDE). The clamp loader
